invariant: INV-66
file: src/p256.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh p256-adx
reason: verify_rs runs the copy's verifier for every value but 0, whatever
  CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX says, so a session on a CPU without BMI2 or ADX dies of
  SIGILL at its first ECDSA P-256 verification. The verdicts stay right.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into the copy's verifier under
  the multiply bit alone, and the qemu lane runs it for x86-64.

--- old
    if ((cpu & CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX) != 0) {
        return p256_adx_verify_rs(pub, msg_hash, r_be, s_be);
--- new
    if (cpu != 0) {
        return p256_adx_verify_rs(pub, msg_hash, r_be, s_be);
